<content><![CDATA[<p>Check your understanding of this lesson. Your answers aren't recorded.</p>
<multiple-choice question="What is the main purpose of render passes (AOVs)?" single-option="" randomize="">
  <input type="checkbox" value="To output separate components, such as diffuse, specular and shadows, for compositing" data-correct="true">
  <input type="checkbox" value="To render faster at lower quality">
  <input type="checkbox" value="To save the image in several file formats">
  <input type="checkbox" value="To preview the scene in the viewport">
</multiple-choice>
<true-false-question question="In a path tracer, raising the sample count usually reduces noise but increases render time.">
  <input type="checkbox" value="True" data-correct="true">
  <input type="checkbox" value="False">
</true-false-question>
<self-check title="Think it through">
  <p slot="question">Your render takes too long. Name three changes that would shorten it, and what each one costs.</p>
  <p>For example: fewer samples with a denoiser (can lose fine detail), fewer light bounces (less realistic indirect light), a lower resolution or render region (less image), or simpler geometry and smaller textures (less detail). Adaptive sampling and GPU rendering can also help.</p>
</self-check>
